<div class="modal fade" id="auctionDuckInfo" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="auctionDuckInfoTitle" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-centered modal-dialog-scrollable">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">
                <h2 class="modal-title h5 d-flex align-items-center" id="auctionDuckInfoTitle"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info me-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>How do the ducks work? <iconify-icon icon="mdi:duck" class="text-warning ms-2 fs-28 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></iconify-icon></h2>
                <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
                <p>The number beside the duck shows how many ducks you’ll have in the duck race for that item.</p>
                <p>When you register for a card or accessory, you start with <strong><span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center text-nowrap align-middle"><iconify-icon icon="mdi:duck" class="text-warning me-2 fs-28" aria-hidden="true"></iconify-icon>×1</span></strong>. You can register for several different items, but you can only have <strong>one active registration per item</strong>.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4 mb-2">How do you get more ducks?</h3>
                <p>When a player successfully bids for an item and receives it from the auction, an admin marks their registration as completed and removes their name from that item’s list. The item is then saved in their player history as <strong>received</strong>.</p>
                <p>Everyone still registered for <strong>that same item</strong> gets <strong>+1 duck</strong>.</p>
                <p>For example, three players register for Mirage Dracula Card:</p>
                <div class="table-responsive">
                    <table class="table table-bordered align-middle">
                        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Player</th><th scope="col">Starting ducks</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>CHKO</td><td><span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center text-nowrap align-middle"><iconify-icon icon="mdi:duck" class="text-warning me-2 fs-28" aria-hidden="true"></iconify-icon>×1</span></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>abuzam</td><td><span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center text-nowrap align-middle"><iconify-icon icon="mdi:duck" class="text-warning me-2 fs-28" aria-hidden="true"></iconify-icon>×1</span></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Serap</td><td><span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center text-nowrap align-middle"><iconify-icon icon="mdi:duck" class="text-warning me-2 fs-28" aria-hidden="true"></iconify-icon>×1</span></td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p>CHKO successfully bids for the card and receives it from the auction. An admin marks CHKO’s registration as completed, and the remaining list becomes:</p>
                <div class="table-responsive">
                    <table class="table table-bordered align-middle">
                        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Player</th><th scope="col">Ducks after CHKO receives the card</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>abuzam</td><td><span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center text-nowrap align-middle"><iconify-icon icon="mdi:duck" class="text-warning me-2 fs-28" aria-hidden="true"></iconify-icon>×2</span></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Serap</td><td><span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center text-nowrap align-middle"><iconify-icon icon="mdi:duck" class="text-warning me-2 fs-28" aria-hidden="true"></iconify-icon>×2</span></td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p>If abuzam successfully bids for and receives the card next, an admin completes their registration, and Serap moves up to <strong><span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center text-nowrap align-middle"><iconify-icon icon="mdi:duck" class="text-warning me-2 fs-28" aria-hidden="true"></iconify-icon>×3</span></strong>.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4 mb-2">Each item has its own duck count</h3>
                <p>Your ducks are counted separately for every item. You could have <strong>×3 for Dracula Card</strong>, <strong>×1 for Angeling Card</strong>, and <strong>×2 for an accessory</strong>.</p>
                <p>Someone receiving Dracula Card only increases the ducks for players still registered for Dracula Card. It does not affect anyone’s duck count for other cards or accessories.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4 mb-2">What if you join the list later?</h3>
                <p>New registrations always start at <strong>×1</strong>, even if other players on the list already have more ducks. You gain extra ducks when another player receives that item and an admin completes their registration while you are still on the list.</p>
                <p>If you receive an item and register for it again later, your new registration starts at <strong>×1</strong>. Your previous receipt stays in your player history.</p>

                <h3 class="h5 mt-4 mb-2">Does having more ducks guarantee a win?</h3>
                <p>No. More ducks give you more entries in the race. If every duck has an equal chance, having more entries improves your chance of winning, but it does not guarantee the result.</p>
                <p>For example, if you have <strong>3 ducks out of 10 ducks in the race</strong>, your chance would be <strong>30%</strong>, assuming every duck has an equal chance.</p>
                <p class="mb-0">The race takes place on the Titania Discord server. Make sure you join! This page records who wants each item, how many ducks they have, and which items they have received. It does not run the race or choose the winner.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-footer">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
